240 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The research project investigates the use of natural language processing \(NLP\) techniques to assist in cooking by suggesting alternative ingredients and generating new recipes. It employs word embedding methods, specifically the Skip-gram model, to assess ingredient similarity, and utilizes language models such as the traditional N-gram and RNN with LSTM for recipe generation. The study analyzed a dataset of 3,433 recipes from various cuisines, revealing the potential of NLP to enhance cooking experiences.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [25]
>>
