/S /P
/E (Classification of Cuisines from Sequentially Structured Recipes)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The study evaluates various algorithms and models for cuisine classification based on recipes. It highlights that Logistic Regression achieved the highest accuracy of 57.70%, but models faced challenges due to a sparse dataset and high bias. Sequential models, particularly Transformers, outperformed traditional statistical models, with the RoBERTa model achieving the best accuracy of 73.3% and a loss of 0.10. The research also utilized LSTMs and emphasized the importance of considering cooking processes and techniques in addition to ingredients for improved classification accuracy.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
